lib
========

A simple, yet powerful, C-based I/O library.

Requirements
------------

- C99 or higher
- MinGW
- MinGW-w64
- MinGW-w64-g++

Building
--------

    mkdir build
    cd build
    cmake ..
    make

Usage
-----

    # include the library
    #include <iostream>

    #include "stdio.h"
    #include "stdlib.h"
    #include "string.h"

    #include "lib.h"

    int main() {
        // create a file handle
        FILE *file = fopen("myfile.txt", "w");

        // create a string to hold the contents of the file
        char buffer[1024];

        // create a pointer to the string
        char *string = buffer;

        // read the contents of the file into the string
        fread(string, 1, 1024, file);

        // write the contents of the string to the file
        fwrite(string, 1, 1024, file);

        // close the file
        fclose(file);

        // display the contents of the file
        printf("Contents of the file: \n%s\n", string);

        // close the file
        fclose(file);

        return 0;
    }

